WEBVTT

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:21.450
<b>Muhyo & Roji's
Bureau of Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.980
X Day, X Month

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:33.980
How much longer, Bico?

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:37.990
The Pacific Ocean

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.960
The island isn't on any map.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.400
The only map is in my head.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.130
That's why I asked.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:43.590
We'll be there soon. Soon...

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:45.600
<i>Magical tools masters.</i>

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.650
<i>Their origins are unknown.</i>

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.710
<i>The various magical tools 
used by magical lawyers,</i>

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:55.000
<i>such as talismans, pens, 
and magical law texts,</i>

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.010
<i>are all created by these masters.</i>

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.830
<i>But in order to protect the 
secrets of their trade,</i>

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.510
<i>we rarely ever see them in person.</i>

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.020
<i>And yet, one of them</i>

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.860
<i>suddenly showed up in front of us.</i>

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:15.780
<b>Muhyo Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.780
A Few Hours Earlier

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.090
<b>Roji's Room</b>

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.120
What's all this noise?

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.030
Huh?!

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.540
Wake up, Muhyo!

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:34.090
Muhyo! Th-There's something 
behind the bookshelf!

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.800
Ugh...

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.300
Huh? Didn't the magic circle 
disappear a long time ago?

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.060
I put it back up afterward.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.940
<b>Article 7 
Magic Prison</b>

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.120
Whew, that startled me.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.740
We're the ones who were startled.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.890
Bico! You little punk!

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.660
Pretty sure I was more startled...

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.360
H-Huh?

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.170
Pardon my asking, but... who are you?

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.320
I am called Bico, the magical tools master.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:17.800
<b>Magical Tools Master 
Abiko Yu</b>

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.220
My real name is Abiko Yu.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:20.570
I've known about you for a long time.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:25.430
Magical Tools Master   Abiko Yu

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:25.430
I've known Muhyo since we attended 
MLS, Magic Law School, together.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:28.020
<b>Magical Tools Master 
Abiko Yu</b>

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.020
Magical tools master?

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.350
What're you doing here?

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:36.160
They say it's a bad omen when a 
magical tools master takes action.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.980
Everyone says so.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.740
The truth is, I need you both 
to come to a magic prison.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.490
Magic prison?

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:49.120
To be precise, Magic Prison No. 18.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:53.060
It's a prison castle where many 
powerful spirits are imprisoned.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:57.790
It's no surprise that a grunt like you 
wouldn't know about magic prisons.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:00.440
They're one of the Magical Law 
Association's top secrets...

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.540
In other words, a black 
mark on their reputation.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.430
I-I see...

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:08.180
There's a shortage of executors.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:13.640
Oh, I did read that there's a growing 
gap between the number of spirits

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.950
and the number of people who 
can deal with them directly.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.610
Which is why they've been using 
talismans to temporarily seal spirits,

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:26.590
but I got a call saying an incident 
occurred at Magic Prison No. 18,

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.620
the prison where my talismans are being used.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:29.550
What?

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:31.290
I couldn't believe my ears.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:35.100
It's the lowest level, where spirits ranked 
with a danger level of A are kept.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.630
So I used the most powerful 
talisman I could produce

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.630
to ensure it would stay sealed, and yet...

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:45.130
The seal on the lowest level was broken?

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.650
And you think it's your fault?

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.920
And you want me to come 
check it out with you?

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:56.140
Hmph. No way. Too much hassle.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:58.570
Or so I'd like to say,

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.260
but I doubt I'll be able 
to sleep if I don't go.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.130
So I will.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:04.460
Really?!

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:06.040
You owe me one.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.670
A magic prison sounds kind of scary, but...

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:13.800
I'll try my hardest to help, Bico-san!

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:20.090
Now

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.160
Disgusting!

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:21.090
Sorry...

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:23.090
I see it!

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.010
That's the island where the magic prison is.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:34.350
Incoming Call

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.350
<b>Yoichi the Perv</b>

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:38.350
Yoichi! How've you been?

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:42.190
Hey. You sound as lively as ever, Nana-chan.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.110
Are your boobs still as nice as ever, too?

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.730
I see you're the same as ever yourself.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.360
Sorry! Don't hang up on me!

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.730
Have you seen the guys lately?

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.840
Yeah, I'm just on my way to see 
them with some donuts now.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:56.360
Seriously? I'm so jealous!

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.890
Did you need to talk to Muhyo-san?

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.570
Yeah, sort of.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:02.630
<i>Then why call me?</i>

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:06.680
<i>If I called him personally, he'd 
think something weird was up.</i>

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:08.380
<b>Muhyo Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:09.560
Next time they go out somewhere, 
could you let me know?

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:11.430
Why only if they go out?

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:16.140
<b>Away on business! 
Sorry for the inconvenience!!</b>

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.140
Well, I just heard something 
that worried me a little...

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:35.100
Is this...

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:42.460
There are people...

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:48.720
<i>Wow, she's really pretty.</i>

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:51.260
Hey!

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.540
You're late, Bico!

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.200
Teacher!

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.140
Huh?!

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.310
Muhyo!

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.310
Stay away from me, woman.

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:08.820
Aw! Your guard's up and 
strong as ever, you cruel boy!

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.160
Wh-Who is she?

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:15.100
This is my teacher, the charismatic 
magical tools master,

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.160
Kurotori Rio-sama!

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.360
I'm Rio. Pleasure to meet you.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.660
Magical Tools Master   Kurotori Rio

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:20.740
Thanks for looking after Bico.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.670
And you're Muhyo's assistant, Roji-san?

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:25.960
Ah... Yes!

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.650
You're adorable...

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:32.470
You're gross, you hag.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:35.960
Gross?! She's the one who made your book!

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:39.220
It's okay, Bico. He was right 
on all but the "hag" part.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.360
What? You made Muhyo's book?

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.640
Th-That's amazing!

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:46.610
Hmph. More importantly, 
why are you even here?

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.610
Why else? I was worried about...

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.820
this very unladylike girl.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.820
<b>Girl</b>

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:55.480
What?! You're a g-g-girl?!

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:00.580
It always was impossible to tell 
until you took off her hat.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.480
But she got all lovey-dovey about her teacher...

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.320
Give it back!

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:06.020
She's always done that, too.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:07.790
Now, Bico...

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:08.550
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:11.160
You two have a job to do.

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:14.130
I'll let the jailers explain things to you.

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:16.490
You are the gentlemen from 
the Muhyo Bureau, yes?

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:19.140
Jailer 
Iwamoto

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:19.140
Jailer 
Maeda

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:19.140
Jailer 
Furuya

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:19.140
Thank you so much for coming.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:22.980
It has been a horrific three days.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.800
Th-There's no reason to talk outside.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:28.760
Why don't we go inside and talk—

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.280
We can't go in!

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:32.490
There's a talisman sealing 
it from the inside.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.160
Let's hear what this is all about.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:44.750
Three Days Ago

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.000
Judge's Assistant   Fujiwara

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:48.000
Huh? Noises coming from the cells?

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.800
Judge   Imai

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.800
Is it not always like this?

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:53.760
It's just a bit excessive today.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:09:00.060
So I was hoping you and your assistant 
could check the cells for us...

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:06.140
You have a point. This 
ruckus is a bit concerning.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:16.380
Th-Thank you so much for doing this!

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:19.470
Maeda-san, will we get 
paid overtime for this?

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:21.880
Don't be imprudent, Fujiwara.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:28.170
Man, it sucks being on 
duty at a magic prison.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.590
All the people here are boring.

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:32.760
It's just another seven days.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.800
Besides, the jailers don't have any powers,

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.880
but they're still doing their best to—

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.080
D-Don't scare me like that.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.230
These are the sounds?

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.600
Hey! If you want something, say so!

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.760
You guys can't come out here 
because of the talisman, anyway!

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.860
Keep acting up, and I'll have you 
sent straight to Hell from here!

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:04.650
Please do that... before <i>it</i> gets here...

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:08.300
It's coming... I-I'm scared...

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.180
"It"... is coming?

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:18.130
Magic Prison  Bottom Level

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.720
O-Oh, no...

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:23.220
The talisman is gone!

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:26.730
Th-This is really bad! This cell is where...

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:27.930
Let's go back!

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.030
R-Right!

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:33.900
What are you doing?! Hurry, Fujiwara!

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.860
I can't! I-I'm so scared, my legs won't...

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.520
P-Please help me!

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.800
Imai-san!

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:50.450
F-Fujiwara...

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:51.210
I'm sorry!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:56.460
It got Fujiwara.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.420
Evacuate everyone from the prison!

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:02.180
H-How can this be?

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:05.440
Emergency! Emergency!

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.180
All employees are to evacuate the premises!

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:09.980
What happened?!

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.870
A talisman was torn off! Run!

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:12.850
It can't be!

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:17.070
Yes, Bico-san, it was your 
talisman. The bottom level.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.260
Yes, I'm leaving immediately.

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.250
Imai-san!

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.000
Imai-sa—

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.420
Everyone run, now!

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:34.670
Imai-san!

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:37.170
What's going on?! Imai-san!

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:39.520
I've sealed it from the inside.

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:41.530
Now the spirit can't get out.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:44.680
It'll probably take two 
days for help to arrive...

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:48.220
With my powers, this is all I can do.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:52.100
Maeda-san, the rest is up to—

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:01.950
<b>Bean Sprout</b>

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:01.950
<b>Onion</b>

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:01.950
<b>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:07.950
<b>Imprisonment in Magic Prinson Cell</b>

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:07.950
<b>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:13.580
I'm certain Judge Imai did that to save us...

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:16.750
Was the talisman she put up...

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:18.660
this one?

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:23.260
Muhyo!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:27.630
She thought she could immobilize 
a spirit from the lowest level

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:29.260
with that piece of scrap?

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:34.420
You're right. A spirit that 
could tear Bico's talisman

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:38.610
could never be sealed by 
the power of a mere judge.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.260
No...

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:43.960
But why isn't the spirit 
coming outside, then?

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:48.820
It's probably been waiting for someone with 
the power to punish spirits to get here.

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:52.660
In other words, it's not 
interested in weaklings.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:58.170
It's been looking forward to 
torturing people like us to death.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:02.440
As payback for the boredom 
it's endured here, you know?

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:11.050
Anything over there?

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:12.880
I can't sense anything.

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:16.160
The offices, the night duty 
room, the stairwell...

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.260
We've checked the entire prison now.

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:20.300
Which means...

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.660
It has to be <i>there</i>.

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:32.660
The magic prison is down this hole?

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:36.240
Because of my talisman...

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.960
That's not why it happened, Bico.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:42.810
This wasn't your fault.

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:49.890
Well, you can save that chat
 for when we get back alive...

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:52.100
from this Hell.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:03.280
This way! This way!

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:08.030
A-Are you sure we should 
close it, Executor Muhyo?

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:11.190
You want the spirit to get outside?

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:14.040
S-See you later...

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.710
In my twenty years working here,

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:28.430
this is the first time I've closed 
this gate with people inside...

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.860
It's so dark, I can't see a thing.

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:37.710
Huh? Guys?

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:39.000
Don't take another step.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.520
Weren't you looking from up there, you idiot?

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:55.320
The walkways are narrow 
here, so please be careful.

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:57.100
R-Right...

00:14:58.180 --> 00:14:59.460
Wait a sec.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.810
Bico-san?

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:07.150
The talisman on the lowest level may 
not have been the only one torn.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:09.840
I think we need to check all of them.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:15.160
True. It's hard to imagine all this 
ectoplasm coming from a single spirit,

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:17.100
but with that one, it's possible.

00:15:17.840 --> 00:15:19.190
"That one"?

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:23.830
Let us out of here, too...

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.790
Let's go, Roji-kun. We need to hurry.

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:29.610
R-Right!

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:32.200
Wait... Please wait...

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:38.120
U-Um, Rio-sensei...

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:41.750
What is the evil spirit on the bottom floor?

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:47.750
Have you heard of a ghost 
called Sophie the Face Ripper?

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:50.220
Face Ripper?!

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:55.630
When she was human, she was 
called the "Masked Girl."

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:57.510
After dying, she became a ghost...

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:03.400
and she ripped off the faces 
of 2,000 people over 500 years,

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:07.690
terrorizing all of Europe. She 
was the worst kind of ghost.

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:11.930
The Association finally 
caught her 20 years ago

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:17.480
and sealed her here, on the lowest 
level of Magic Prison 18.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:24.540
What? So this Sophie is...

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:27.000
Yep, that's the story.

00:16:28.310 --> 00:16:30.090
W-We've got trouble!

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.970
This cell has no talisman!

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:34.400
Does that mean Sophie—

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:36.550
This isn't her cell... but...

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:44.260
It's definitely true that Sophie got out.

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:47.830
My skin... My skin...

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:53.190
That's the evil spirit that 
collects human eyes, Red-Eye!

00:16:55.410 --> 00:17:00.680
Give me back... my face!

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:03.680
Perfect timing. Let's have a warm-up.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:05.830
You can't use magical law wastefully, Muhyo!

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:06.790
Huh?

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:07.850
This way, everyone!

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.220
H-Hey!

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.750
Bico, give Roji-kun his!

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:12.500
Right!

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:16.890
Using these talismans will make 
your spells more powerful.

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:19.140
Use them to make a spirit barrier!

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:23.270
But wouldn't you or Rio-san 
be better at that than me?

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:26.160
My face!

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:29.770
Magic tools masters can make 
these, but we can't use them!

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:30.770
Huh?

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:34.280
Give me back my face!

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:39.530
B-But... I...

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:42.810
Magic Binding Spell!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.040
You're a medium?!

00:17:45.340 --> 00:17:47.000
The talisman misfired?

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:52.670
Give me back my face! Give me back my face!

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:53.930
Hurry!

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:57.180
The spirit barrier is an easier 
spell than magic binding!

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.680
My face!

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.070
It worked...

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:15.360
I thought that was a strong 
talisman, but the barrier's weak.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.640
It won't withstand another attack!

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:19.370
Quick, use magic binding, too!

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:20.070
Right!

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:24.900
<i>With this talisman, I should be able 
to do the Magic Binding Spell, too...</i>

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:27.080
Huh?!

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.200
Why?

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.460
Roji-kun isn't strong enough.

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:35.430
He's incompatible with your strong talisman.

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:38.630
Give me back my face!

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:39.970
The talisman withstood the spirit 
barrier since it's a weak spell,

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:43.500
but a magic tool's power needs 
to be equal to its user's.

00:18:45.990 --> 00:18:49.730
In your current mental state, you 
can't use your powers to the fullest.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.450
Try using my talisman.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:55.670
I believe in you, Roji-kun.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:00.350
My face!

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:07.350
M-Magic Binding Spell!

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.100
I-I did it...

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:23.900
I felt... I felt it work!

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.250
Rio-sensei!

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.770
Wh-What?

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:40.930
Oh, no...

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:42.780
It's kibble now.

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:45.140
Kibble?!

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:48.180
How many spirits have gotten out?

00:19:57.950 --> 00:19:59.020
What's that?!

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:01.440
A mass of abandoned dog spirits,

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:02.590
the Rain Dog.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.100
Bico!

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:12.600
The Rain Dog's virus got to her!

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.990
We have to destroy the virus, quickly!

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:15.860
Muhyo!

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:17.800
Tsk! Get back!

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:30.620
Back us up with a spirit barrier!

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:34.030
But I can only do it with 
Rio-sensei's talismans!

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:44.380
Is this... Silver Armor?

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:47.040
I threw it up in a hurry.

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:48.760
It won't last long.

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:50.700
Bico!

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:55.650
Bico! This isn't good!

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:58.150
Her eyes... Does this mean...

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:01.150
A spirit virus, huh?

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:08.620
It's all right. I won't let it happen.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.740
Don't worry, Bico.

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:16.010
On my name as Rio the magical 
tools master, I won't let you die!

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:53.550
Let's learn about magical law!

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:53.550
(with video)

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:53.550
<b>Kusano Jiro 
"We don't have any sponsors!"</b>

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:53.550
Subscribe

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:53.550
LawTube!

00:22:53.550 --> 00:22:57.840
Today, Bico-san will teach us 
about magical tools masters!

00:22:53.550 --> 00:23:02.810
<b>About Magical Tools Masters</b>

00:22:57.840 --> 00:22:59.150
I'm Bico.

00:22:59.150 --> 00:23:00.640
We magical tools masters

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:05.800
make and fix the magical tools 
that executors and judges use.

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:09.000
Wow, there's a lot in here.

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:10.730
Hey, what's this?

00:23:10.730 --> 00:23:13.200
Oh, that's my lunch.

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:14.090
And this?

00:23:14.090 --> 00:23:16.200
Changes of clothes for a week.

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:17.270
And this?

00:23:17.270 --> 00:23:19.720
A picture of my teacher, Rio...

00:23:19.720 --> 00:23:22.040
Wow... Then how about this?

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:23.370
Oh, th-that's not...

00:23:23.370 --> 00:23:24.320
Aw, what is it?

00:23:24.320 --> 00:23:26.670
Don't! Don't! Don't look!

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:27.870
Shut up!

00:23:27.870 --> 00:23:28.830
Muhyo?!

00:23:28.830 --> 00:23:29.970
Why?

00:23:30.530 --> 00:23:35.220
It takes on another's form 
and lives their life.

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:40.810
Are you talking about someone 
in the magic prison?

00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:45.480
Next time on <i>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau 
of Supernatural Investigation</i>,

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:47.360
Article 8:

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:48.940
"Becoming Someone Else."

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:51.780
Magical law will be enforced.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:54.950
<b>Article 8 
Becoming Someone Else</b>
